Since C16 requires n >= 16, any {C4,C8}-avoiding delta>=3 graph on n <= 15 would refute Erdos-Gyarfas outright. For n <= 12: none exist (this census). Royle/Markstrom (cited): none for n <= 16; cubic counterexamples need n >= 30; Markstrom found 24-vertex cubic graphs avoiding C4 and C8 but containing C16.

